        <headline>Gale Warning issued September 25 at 2:48AM EDT until September 26 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Upton NY</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Small Craft Advisory, northeast winds 20 to 25
kt and waves 3 to 6 feet. For the Gale Warning, north winds 25
to 35 kt with gusts up to 40 kt and waves 4 to 7 feet expected.

* WHERE...New York Harbor, including Raritan Bay and Sandy Hook
Bay.

* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, until 6 AM EDT early this
morning. For the Gale Warning, from 2 PM this afternoon to 8
PM EDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous waves which could
capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should alter plans to avoid these hazardous conditions.
Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for hazardous conditions.</instruction>
